## Objective
- Autonomously hunt valid, reproducible, high-impact bugs in authorized scope (`data/targets.txt` = 86 top-level routes on `console.byteplus.com`) following `skills/AGENT.md`, and report confirmed findings in `result/`.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn/aaii-aautomattionn`
- Scope: only the listed `https://console.byteplus.com/...` top-level routes + same-origin JS/APIs required to exercise them. No sibling domains, CDNs as test targets, or unrelated paths. `/datafinder` (and its `/lark-verify` sink) is NOT in the list → out of scope.
- Test creds (`creds/test-account.txt`):
  - Account A: `adoringjepsen1@fearlessmails.com` / `Acd3423@#345566` → AccountID `3000823185`, name `test-user-123`
  - Account B: `testt456` / `Acd3423@#345` → AccountID `3001021825`
- Chrome DevTools MCP connected (`http://127.0.0.1:9222`); pages: 1 = main account A, 2 = isolated `redirtest` (A), 3 = isolated `acctB` (B).
- Session start `2026-10-29T03:52:40Z`; budget ~5h35m active, hard timeout 5h55m.
- Auth uses cookies incl. HttpOnly `digest`/`userInfo`; CSRF token readable via `document.cookie` `csrfToken`. Authenticated API calls need header `x-csrf-token: <csrfToken>`; in-page `fetch(...,{credentials:'include',headers:{'x-csrf-token':tok,'accept':'application/json'}})`.
- `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` currently empty (headers only).
- `rg` is NOT installed in this environment; use Python regex or `grep` instead.
- Prior-agent leftover IAM users in account A (6 users, `bb-dts-pm-*`, description "Authorized DTS postMessage takeover test", created 2026-08-27) indicate an earlier DTS postMessage investigation; no notes found in `vulnebleti`.
- Git HEAD prior-run artifacts (`result/TEST-NOTIFICATION.md`, `result/logs/diagnostics-index.txt`, `result/logs/opencode/opencode.log`) contain no prior findings (notification test only).

## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight done; wrote `result/logs/session.md` and `result/scope.md`; created `result/{client-side,server-side,findings,inventory,logs}`.
- Logged in as account A and B; captured AccountIDs.
- Negative results (verified):
  - `/auth/login/?redirectURI=https://example.com/` → after login lands `/home` (no open redirect). `javascript:` URI gets 403 at edge.
  - `/signin/login?redirectURI=https://example.com` 302 → `signin.byteplus.com/auth/login?redirectURI=...` (chain not fully tested).
  - BFF GraphQL `VolcAPI_getVolcAdminAccountInfo` ignores client-supplied `AccountID` (returns own `3000823185`).
  - `ListInMail`: `DataScope=All` rejected `InvalidParamError`; `AccountId`/`AccountID` ignored (returns own 24 msgs).
  - `GetInMailInfo` with B's msg ID `30961034` from A → "站内信不存在".
  - `GetTicket` with B's ticket `I-2026080515360001` from A → `Forbidden`; also with added `AccountID`/`AccountId`/`SubmitterID` → `Forbidden`.
  - `ListTicketConversation` cross-account → blocked.
  - IAM BOLA: `GET /api/top/iam/ap-southeast-1/2018-01-01/ListUsers?Limit=1000&Offset=0` returns own 6 users; adding `AccountId`/`AccountID=3001021825` ignored. `GetUser?UserName=testtttt` (B) → `UserNotExist`; `GetUser?UserId=97235517` → `InvalidParameter: Invalid Parameter: ID`; `ListRoles?...&AccountId=3001021825` ignored (returns own 18 roles). `GetAccount?AccountId=3001021825` also tested (own data).
- Captured route manifest for 85 routes to `/tmp/routes_apps.json` and full HTML-derived JS URLs to `/tmp/routes_js.json`; 379 unique product JS URLs, 151 non-vendor files downloaded to `/tmp/pjs` (182M).
- Scanned `/tmp/pjs` for `location.*`/`window.open` sinks, `addEventListener("message")` handlers, and `decodeURIComponent` near sinks → only framework/SDK boilerplate, no confirmed in-scope DOM XSS.
- Read `vulnebleti/Xss/console-search/*`; confirmed `/lark-verify` datafinder sink is out of scope.
- Workorder ticket conversation renders server HTML via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML:{__html:(0,b.dW)(e)}`; `dW` = module `73868` function `p` = linkifier only, does NOT strip tags/attrs.
- Verified in live DOM on ticket `I-2026102903040001`: `<img src="x">` and `<style>a{color:red;}</style>` present inside `.ticket-conversation-module__commentContentHtml--EkZ_9`.
- CSP header on `console.byteplus.com` only `frame-ancestors ...` (no `script-src`), so inline handlers would run if preserved.
- Server-side sanitizer mapping (live submissions to ticket `I-2026102903050001`):
  - `<img src=x onerror="...">` stored as `<img src="x">` (event handler stripped).
  - Multi-tag probe stored as: `<b>P1</b>x<a href="" rel="noopener noreferrer noopener noreferrer">j1</a><a href="" ...>j2</a><video src=""></video><details open="">sd</details>` — `iframe`, `object`, `embed`, `svg`, `math`, `meta`, `base`, `link`, `form`, `input`, `srcdoc` stripped; `javascript:`/`data:` hrefs normalized to empty; `video src` emptied.
  - Surviving: `b`, `a` (href normalized), `video` (src emptied), `details`/`summary`, and earlier `div/style/class/id/img`.
- Ticket statuses: `I-2026102903040001` and `I-2026102903030001` are closed → `CreateTicketConversation` returns `RequestInvalid: 工单状态已发生变化，请刷新页面`. `I-2026102903050001` is open and accepts comments.
